---
import Slide from "../../components/Slide.astro"
// import Link from "../../components/Link.astro"
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro"
import { Image } from 'astro:assets'
import cubic_diff from "../../img/maths/cubic-diff.png"
---
<Slide t1="Calculus">
    <ul>
        <li class="fragment">The study of change and motion in mathematics</li>
        <li class="fragment"><span class="text-yellow">Differential calculus</span>:
            slopes and rates</li>
        <li class="fragment"><span class="text-yellow">Integral calculus</span>:
            areas and accumulation</li>
        <li class="fragment">(We are mostly concerned with differential calculus)</li>
    </ul>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="Calculus Examples">
    <ul>
        <li class="fragment">Consider distance (in a straight line)</li>
        <li class="fragment">What do we call the rate of change (differential)
            of distance?</li>
        <li class="fragment">What do we call the rate of change of <em>that</em>?</li>
    </ul>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="P5 Worked Examples">
    <ul>
        <li class="fragment">We are going to plot some new equations (curves)</li>
        <li class="fragment">We are also going to plot the rate of change
            of these equations</li>
        <li class="fragment">i.e. we are going to <em>differentiate</em> them&mdash;in code</li>
        <li class="fragment">(Memo: don't forget to try the trigonometric functions)</li>
    </ul>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="Cubic and Differential">
    <div class="flex justify-center items-center">
        <Image
            src={ cubic_diff }
            alt="Cubic and Differential"
            height="400"
            width="400" />
    </div>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="Cubic and Differential">
    <ul>
        <li class="fragment">The black line is the cubic equation
            \( y = x^3 - x^2 \)
        </li>

        <li class="fragment">The red line is quadratic, the differential ("slope") of the cubic:
            \( y = 3x^2 - 2x \)

        </li>
    </ul>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="Calculating the Differential">
    <p>How do we calculate the differential graph points?</p>

    <ul>
        <li class="fragment">Calculate the <em>difference</em> between each <code>y</code>
            value and the previous one</li>
        <li class="fragment">Plot this sequence of values&mdash;the differences in the
            <code>y</code> values of the original curve
        </li>
    </ul>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="Differential Code">
    <div class="text-sm-1">
        <CodeBlock lang="javascript" height="450px" lines="*|1-4|8-14|16-18">
            { `
// Plot the y of the original curve (mapping to pixel position):
let yPixel = map(y, -1, 1, height/2, -height/2)
fill(0) // Black.
circle(xPixel, yPixel, 10)

// If there's a previous y, calculate the difference (mapping
// to pixel position also):
if (previous_y != null) {
    yPixel = map(y - previous_y,
                 -0.01, 0.01,
                 height/2, -height/2)
    fill(255, 0, 0) // Red.
    circle(xPixel, yPixel, 10)
}

// Remember this y position: it'll be the previous position
// the next time round the loop:
previous_y = y
            `.trim() }
        </CodeBlock>
    </div>
</Slide>

